olimits_{	heta} igl{(}W,\ell^{\prime}(	heta) igr{)}=0 instead of  1 : the two sides of (13.1) are  rac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}	heta}\mathbb{E}_{	heta}(W)=1 on the left and \int W(x) rac{\partial}{\partial	heta}f(x;	heta)\,\mathrm{d}x=-(n/	heta)% \mathbb{E}_{	heta}(W)=-n on the right, and the difference is the contribution of the moving boundary of the support. There is no contradiction: the inequality has hypotheses, and the uniform model violates these hypotheses. Super-efficiency is a property of models where the parameter is an endpoint of the support, where a single observation near the endpoint can be used to estimate 	heta much more accurately than for a regular model. In lecture 16 we will prove the consistency of  M using a direct argument. In lecture 17 we will see that the limiting distribution of  M is not normal. In lecture 15 we will use simulation to demonstrate the 1/n^{2} decay of the variance. Summary. •​Under the conditions of section 11.1, all unbiased estimators  W for g(	heta) satisfy \mathop{\mathrm{Var}}
